@startuml
title SCAN: a later request overtakes a blocked request

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 150

participant "Philosopher P0" as P0
participant "Philosopher P1" as P1
participant "Philosopher P2" as P2
participant "Critical section\n+ central queue" as CS
participant "Event(req0)" as E0
participant "Event(req2)" as E2

P0 -> CS: lock()
P0 -> CS: enqueue(req0)
CS -> CS: req0 cannot be granted\n(forks are busy)
CS --> P0: unlock()
P0 -> E0: sem_timedwait(timeout)

P1 -> CS: lock()
P1 -> CS: enqueue(req1)
CS -> CS: req1 cannot be granted
CS --> P1: unlock()
P1 -> P1: wait on its event

P2 -> CS: lock()
P2 -> CS: enqueue(req2)
CS -> CS: dispatch_locked()\nscan queue from front
CS -> CS: req0 blocked, skip
CS -> CS: req1 blocked, skip
CS -> CS: req2 can be granted\novertakes++
CS -> E2: sem_post()
CS --> P2: unlock()

E2 --> P2: wake up
P2 -> CS: lock()
CS --> P2: req2 = GRANTED
CS --> P2: unlock()
P2 -> P2: EATING

note over P0,E0: req0 still waits.\nThis demonstrates possible\nstarvation in SCAN mode.

@enduml
